  "name": "Follow up webinar attendees and no-shows with two different campaigns",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Follow up webinar attendees and no-shows with two different campaigns\n\n### How it works\nTwo audiences, two messages. After the event, POST JSON with webinar_title, recording_url and attendees (email, first_name, last_name, company, attended, minutes_watched) to the webhook. The workflow splits the list. Attendees join your follow-up campaign with {{webinar_title}} and {{minutes_watched}} as variables. Registrants who did not attend join your replay campaign with {{recording_url}}. Every address is checked and only valid emails join; people already in a campaign are not added twice.\n\nYour own contacts cost no credits.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Pick the campaigns in **Add attendees to follow-up** and **Add no-shows to replay**.\n4. Write the variables into your emails.\n5. POST the attendee list to the production URL of **Attendee list received**.\n\n### Customization\nAdd a third path for people who watched less than ten minutes.",
        "height": 609,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
